---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ConstellationVisual from "../components/ConstellationVisual.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout>
  <section class="hero-section">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <span class="eyebrow">PUBLIC BETA · MARKDOWN-FIRST · PRIVACY-FIRST</span>
      <h1>Turn scattered notes into <span>connected context.</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">
        A second brain that keeps your knowledge in plain Markdown, stores it in
        your own Google Drive, and helps you rediscover the relationships between ideas.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button primary large" href={`${base}app/`}>Open MindContext <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="button secondary large" href="#how-it-works"><span aria-hidden="true">◎</span> How it works</a>
      </div>
      <div class="trust-row" aria-label="MindContext beta facts">
        <span>✓ Free to use</span>
        <span>✓ No separate MindContext account</span>
        <span>✓ Your files stay yours</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ConstellationVisual />
  </section>

  <section class="section feature-section" id="features">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">BUILT AROUND YOUR KNOWLEDGE</span>
      <h2>A workspace designed to stay open.</h2>
      <p>MindContext adds useful projections around your notes without turning them into proprietary data.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="feature-icon">▱</span>
        <h3>Your Drive</h3>
        <p>Use your own Google Drive. MindContext uses narrow file-scoped access instead of owning your storage.</p>
        <a href={`${base}privacy/`}>How storage works →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="feature-icon">▤</span>
        <h3>Markdown-first</h3>
        <p>Notes remain ordinary Markdown with open, Obsidian-compatible conventions for links and structure.</p>
        <a href={`${base}docs/`}>Explore Markdown support →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="feature-icon">◇</span>
        <h3>Privacy-first</h3>
        <p>Search indexes and knowledge projections are local and rebuildable. Your note content is not a MindContext cloud database.</p>
        <a href={`${base}privacy/`}>Read the privacy model →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="feature-icon">✣</span>
        <h3>Plugins-ready</h3>
        <p>The architecture is being designed around explicit capabilities so future extensions do not need your raw storage credentials.</p>
        <a href={`${base}plugins/`}>See the plugin direction →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section how-section" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="section-heading narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">HOW IT WORKS</span>
      <h2>Your files are the source of truth.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>Connect Drive</h3><p>Authorize MindContext with Google Drive's narrow <code>drive.file</code> permission.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>Write naturally</h3><p>Create Markdown notes, wikilinks, properties, tasks, code, tables, math and diagrams.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>Connect context</h3><p>Backlinks, graph and search are derived locally from the files you already own.</p></article>
      <article><span>04</span><h3>Stay portable</h3><p>Leave MindContext whenever you want and your Markdown remains understandable elsewhere.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section pricing-section" id="pricing">
    <div class="pricing-card">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">PRICING</span>
        <h2>Free to use. Open by design.</h2>
        <p>MindContext is currently free. There is no MindContext storage subscription: your Drive remains your storage.</p>
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li>✓ Core beta features</li>
        <li>✓ Your own Google Drive</li>
        <li>✓ No separate MindContext account</li>
        <li>✓ Open-source codebase</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section plugins-preview">
    <div class="section-heading split-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">FUTURE PLUGIN ECOSYSTEM</span>
        <h2>Extend your thinking.</h2>
        <p>Plugins are a product direction, not a finished marketplace yet. The goal is to add capabilities without changing who owns your data.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${base}plugins/`}>Plugin roadmap →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="plugin-grid">
      <article><span>◎</span><strong>Web Clipper</strong><small>Concept · capture sources from the web</small></article>
      <article><span>▦</span><strong>Calendar</strong><small>Concept · connect events and notes</small></article>
      <article><span>✦</span><strong>Local AI</strong><small>Planned · ask your knowledge locally</small></article>
      <article><span>＋</span><strong>Community</strong><small>Future · capability-based extensions</small></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section final-cta">
    <span class="eyebrow">PUBLIC BETA</span>
    <h2>Start building context you still own.</h2>
    <p>Use the beta, tell us what breaks, and help shape the next version of MindContext.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button primary large" href={`${base}app/`}>Open MindContext →</a>
      <a class="button secondary large" href={`${base}feedback/`}>Send feedback</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
